status GREEN on what was run, and the roster reading is PARTIAL and named as such. Every guard whose watched files intersect this round is GREEN on metal: itinerary_list, index_row_bound, ascii_document, link_text_promise, unshared_citation, two_rooms_doorway, tracked_link. The cold roster pass was launched with --cadence-slice 1 and stood at 80 guards, zero red, STILL IN FLIGHT at the commit; its run_verdict was not read. I held HEAD still for it through the whole round and it did not reach its verdict inside the lap, so the send names the partial reading rather than claiming a full one. A peer's next cold pass reads this tree whole.
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- the third door is unanswered and far stronger than when it was asked. The steady state is not dispatch-neutral after all: every build re-hashes its own output, so a baseline rye pays 79 ms against 30 on a 10 MB output, forever, beside the three quarters of a second a cold start costs once. Whether rye patches a vendored rye/lib/std is a fork decision only he opens.
